    "title": "Encoded payload decoded and piped to a shell",
    "desc": "Encoded data was decoded and fed straight into a shell - a decoder (base64 -d, base32 -d, xxd -r, uudecode, openssl ... -d) piped into sh/bash/zsh/dash, or wrapped in eval / a $(...) substitution. This is the deobfuscate-and-run pattern (MITRE T1140 into T1059): the next stage is carried as base64/hex so it slips past anything reading the command line, then decoded and executed in one breath. It is rarely anything but malicious - a human or a script with a real payload runs the file, it does not pipe a decode into a shell - so this fires host-wide, whoever runs it. agent_decode catches an agent account merely decoding (a softer, account-scoped signal); this is the run.",
